msgid "Zwift does not find the sensors"
msgstr ""

#: tretlager/kde/qml/SensorsPage.qml:199
msgid ""
"The bridge must be running. In Zwift, select “Wahoo KICKR …” or “Wahoo HRM "
"…” under Paired Devices."
msgstr ""

#: tretlager/kde/qml/SensorsPage.qml:200
msgid "Heart rate far too high"
msgstr ""

#: tretlager/kde/qml/SensorsPage.qml:201
msgid ""
"Moisten the electrodes, tighten the strap and wear only one strap. If that "
"does not help, replace the strap's battery."
msgstr ""

#: tretlager/kde/qml/SensorsPage.qml:202
msgid "Device stays at “Searching for the device…”"
msgstr ""

#: tretlager/kde/qml/SensorsPage.qml:203
msgid ""
"Pedal briefly or unclip the strap for a moment; the bridge searches every "
"ten seconds."
msgstr ""

#: tretlager/kde/qml/SensorsPage.qml:204
msgid "Device never connects"
msgstr ""

#: tretlager/kde/qml/SensorsPage.qml:205
msgid ""
"Some sensors do not get along with certain Bluetooth chips. Tretlager "
"reports known cases on the device; a USB Bluetooth dongle selected as the "
"Bluetooth adapter helps then."
msgstr ""

#: tretlager/kde/qml/SensorsPage.qml:206
msgid "Connection drops often"
msgstr ""

#: tretlager/kde/qml/SensorsPage.qml:207
msgid ""
"Bluetooth does not travel well through walls. Move the computer closer to "
"the trainer or place a USB Bluetooth dongle on an extension cable next to "
"the trainer."
msgstr ""

